---
description: codegen — wire emitters, the go-server inspector schema descriptor, separate immutable Go content views and finalized bundles, physics writer bindings, templates, integration output ownership and containment.
globs:
  - codegen/**/*.go
  - codegen/**/*.tmpl
alwaysApply: false
---

# `codegen`

`go_inspector.go` emits go-server `inspector_schema.go` as a `wire.Schema` literal from `EntityData.ProtoWireLayout` and the resolved `EntityUpdate` envelope; bits come from the delta layout (tick vars), never from `AllVars`. The descriptor is validated at bake time and imports `<golem_import>/inspector/wire`.

Opt-in portable content produces only Go-server `Definitions.go` and `ContentDefinitions.json`, selected by `integration_outputs.go`. `go_content.go` emits eagerly decoded private `Content<Type>` records, typed reference lookups and copied collection accessors; no backing maps/slices escape. It imports the canonical independent `golem/content` package even when `golem_import` selects a consumer runtime facade. `LoadDefinitions` always requires the finalized schema hash and validates explicit imports before publication. Content generation validates names before any bake output and preserves protocol/world descriptors, existing catalog behavior and the legacy snapshot fingerprint. Optional fields return presence separately from zero values; references resolve by stable content identity, including declared imported catalogs, without recursive materialization. Keep consumer factories, lifecycle creation and behavior outside this generator.

Opt-in `EntityData.Physics` emits only Go-server `SetPhysicsRotation(physics3d.Quat)`, `SetPhysicsVelocity(linear, angular physics3d.Vec3)` and `SetPhysicsActive(bool)` interfaces. Rotation/velocity groups update ordinary fields under one entity lock, mark only changed tick bits and increment revision once per changed group; activation delegates to its ordinary setter. Keep fields ordinary in Go/JS/C# codecs, models and snapshots, with unchanged owner redaction and no automatic body attachment. Bindings are resolved by schema, never inferred from field names. Generated-consumer tests share encoded state bytes across Go/JS/C# and preserve the proto/fingerprint baseline. Temporary Go consumers explicitly replace all required local nested modules, including physics3d, without adding tracked replacements.

`Bake` orchestrates proto output plus per-integration generation from `schema` DTOs.

Consume schema's resolved envelope variants, entity wire fields, scalar/collection metadata and catalog item/key metadata; do not allocate tags or repeat type/key lookup. Legacy DTO adaptation belongs at generation boundaries. `codec_metadata.go` contains backend input adapters, not YAML policy or a universal message IR. Language-specific reader/writer mappings, omit-zero guards, public shapes and operation availability stay in codegen.

`go_payload.go`, `js_payload.go` and `cs_payload.go` each share ordinary command/event emission. `envelope_codecs.go` has one emitter per language over ordered variants. Go retains encode/decode for all envelopes; JS/C# command envelopes encode only, other envelopes decode only. Preserve Go's last recognized oneof versus JS/C#'s separate properties. `scalar_encode.go` shares JS/C# scalar guards between ordinary/custom messages; Go retains its own scalar helper. Go entity and world collection emission share element/map-entry algorithms with explicit ordinary/delta presence; nil/undefined/null means absent and a present empty delta collection means clear.

`goFullStateProjection` plus the `fullStateLiteral` template share authoritative/public state construction at generation time. Preserve the wrappers' locks, revision capture, shallow collection references, owner-only tick/once redaction and serialization after unlocking. Keep compact serialization and dirty-mask deltas separate; add no generated runtime identifiers for this helper.

Compatibility evidence lives in the resolution baseline, characterization and generated-consumer tests. Freeze supported wire bytes, public APIs and fingerprint preimages; retain known string/bytes-list framing differences, empty-custom-element behavior, Go unknown map-entry behavior, C# scalar-map default inference and Go tick-bytes limitations until separately reviewed corrections. `GOLEM_REQUIRE_CONSUMERS=1` makes missing compiler/runtime prerequisites fail rather than skip; `GOLEM_CONSUMER_RACE=1` runs generated Go consumers with the race detector.

`RemoveIntegration` only supports shared-only targets without extra emitters or finalizers. It preflights known output names, regular files, the generated header and resolved project containment before removing those files. It must never recursively delete an output directory or alter consumer configuration.

Templates live under `codegen/templates/` and are embedded with `go:embed`.

`integration_outputs.go` owns integration defaults, output names/roles, optional selection and historical JS intermediate recognition. Successful JS finalization removes only top-level regular recognized intermediates bearing the Golem generated header; preserve declarations, unmarked files, unreadable files and nonregular entries. The temporary compiler config is handled separately. `integration.go` preserves the public compatibility projection. Keep descriptors read-only and decorate per-integration entity DTO copies. The relative containment predicate is shared; bridge removal resolves symlinks and rejects Rel failures, while Threlte validation remains lexical with its existing error policy.

`entities.proto` always declares `SpaceChanged{uint32 space=1; uint64 transition=2}`, `SpaceSettled{uint64 transition=1}` and `WorldCleared{string name=1}` as `ServerMessage` fields 4, 5 and 6, independent of the schema; they are runtime envelope fields, so the schema fingerprint is unaffected while the proto template baseline hashes include them. `go_proto.go`, `js_proto.go`, and `csharp_proto.go` generate lightweight codecs for consumers. Optional checked protocol constant sets are emitted in the existing entities outputs as Go untyped constants, TypeScript `as const` objects/unions, and C# static string classes; they are not protobuf fields and do not alter `entities.proto`. Keep Go, JS, and C# client targets conceptually parallel.

**Go server entities (`templates/go_server/server.go.tmpl`):** each `Synced*` carries a runtime-only unexported `srv *golem.Server` plus exported `BindServer` / `Server()` (not wire/snapshot state). `Server()` may be nil before `CreateEntity`; wrapper types embedding `*Synced*` inherit both methods. When `EntityData.Collider` is set, emit `Collider()` (2D) or `Collider3D()` (3D) from schema shape/layer/trigger; wrappers inherit and may override intentionally. When `HasOwnerVars`, emit `OwnerScopedEntity` (`PublicFullUpdate` omitting owner-only tick/once fields, `PublicReplicationMask` clearing owner-only tick bits via `*OwnerOnlyMask`); keep authoritative `FullState`/`FullUpdate` unchanged for persistence and owner delivery. Do not emit those methods for entities without owner-only vars.

**Go server shared (`templates/go_server/shared.go.tmpl`):** when `SharedData.Collision` is set, `Runtime` includes `Layers`+`EnableCollision` (2D) or `Layers3D`+`EnableCollision3D` (3D) that call `MustCollisionBackend`/`MustCollisionBackend3D` (nil panics before any Server setter), build the YAML named matrix, bind the backend, and call `SetCollisionBackend`/`SetCollisionLayers` (or 3D equivalents). The same config also emits `EnableSpaceCollision(space golem.SpaceID, backend) *golem.CollisionLayers` (or `EnableSpaceCollision3D` returning `*golem.CollisionLayers3D`), which builds the same matrix, installs backend and layers through `Server.Space(space)` setters, returns the layers and stores them in `Layers`/`Layers3D` only for space 0; `EnableCollision` stays unchanged. Omit those fields/methods when there is no collision config so projects without collision still compile. Always emit `Runtime.LoadSnapshotIfExists` and blocking `Runtime.RunSnapshotAutosave` (plus unexported `startSnapshotAutosave` / `runSnapshotAutosave` for injectable ticker/ticks/save in tests; validate ctx/interval before ticker creation; check `ctx.Err` before each save); keep `context`/`errors`/`os`/`time` imports valid with or without entities/commands/events/world/collision. Do not add these helpers to non-Go-server client templates. The generated `EventBroadcaster` sends every event, stream delivery included, through `Server.SendServerEvent` / `BroadcastServerEvent` with the event's `DeliveryConst` (`golem.EventStream` produces the same wrapped bytes as the old raw `Send`/`BroadcastEvent`), so the runtime's space-switch event hold and stream-only gate apply to every generated event; never emit raw `srv.Send` / `srv.BroadcastEvent` / `WrapServerEvent` for events.

`codegen/` imports config and template data from `schema`; it should not define YAML schema structs or reimplement schema loading.

When adding an integration, register its output specification in `integration_outputs.go` and add its templates and any `GenerateExtra` or `Finalize` hooks here. Integrations may be shared-only by omitting `Template`/`FileNamer` and emitting only `SharedTemplates`. Full clients (`go-client`, `js-client`, `csharp-client`) own generated managers/codecs; engine integrations (`phaser`, `threlte`, `unity`, `ebiten`) should stay thin and depend on the matching full client output.

Generated Go/JS/C# world managers expose `ClearWorld(name)` / `clearWorld(name)` keyed by the world type name (`WorldName`, the schema's PascalCase name): it resets that field to nil/undefined/null and fires its `On<Name>Cleared` / `on<Name>Cleared` listeners only when a value was held; unknown names are ignored. The C# manager implements `IWorldClearer`; the Go manager satisfies `golemclient.WorldClearer`; the JS manager satisfies the optional `WorldManagerLike.clearWorld`. Threlte world stores subscribe to both the update and the cleared listener.

`threlte` emits only `GolemThrelte.ts`, with typed manager adapters, reactive bindings, component props and complete component/headless registrations. It reuses generated JS entities/world/events/commands and never generates Svelte components, codecs, or presentation choices. The application's Svelte toolchain compiles this bridge; there is no integration finalizer. `threlte_config.go` validates its JS dependency and separate output before generation. Shared-only removal applies unchanged.

Generated Go/JS/C# entity managers share removal between wire removal and clear within each language: remove membership, invoke the entity hook, then notify the manager. Keep wire revision/tombstone checks outside that helper; equal revisions are accepted. Clear snapshots IDs and resets revisions only after callbacks finish. Go compact updates delegate to the ordinary typed delta application after decoding and restoring header IDs/revisions. A compact record for an unknown entity (datagrams can overtake the stream spawn) is copied and held, at most 256 per manager. The eviction order lists each entity with held records once (Go slice / C# `List<long>` / JS `Map` insertion order); dropping an entity's records (replay, wire removal, eviction) also removes it from the order. At the cap every record of the oldest entity is evicted and the single-slot Go/C# `OnResyncNeeded` callback or multicast JS `onResyncNeeded` listeners receive its ID (runtimes send EntityResync). A new spawn replays its held records through `ApplyCompactUpdate` after the spawn callbacks, so the revision check drops older ones, while wire removal and Clear discard them. `Clear` advances `clearEpoch`; the spawn path, each replay iteration and the resync callback check it, so a callback that clears stops the replay and holds nothing more. **Pending resyncs:** when an eviction reports an entity (only with a resync callback/listener registered), the manager records it in `pendingResync` / `_pendingResync` with the newest evicted record's revision (read from the held frames' headers) and a retry count. An applied full state with at least that revision forgets it (an older spawn does not), as do an applied wire removal and `Clear`. A full state rejected as stale (`isStale` in `applyState`) for a pending entity requests the resync again, at most `maxResyncRetries` / `MaxResyncRetries` (3) times, then forgets it; the server's recovery full state can be overtaken by a newer datagram. Go-server entities emit `BumpStateRevision` (locked revision increment, no dirty bits) for `Server.SetOwner`.
